Recommendation
--------------
This repository mixes two kinds of material, so a dual license is common:

- Source code (Python examples and projects): MIT License
  https://opensource.org/license/mit
- Written content (articles, diagrams, notes): Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0)
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

If you plan to sell course material later, consider CC BY-NC 4.0 for the written content instead.

To apply: replace this file with the full license text(s) and add the chosen license to README.md.
